  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b3_u09_l2_g1",
      "pattern": "A/V-(ㄴ/는)다 (yozma uslub, 한다체)",
      "meaning_uz": "Kundalik, maqola, blog uchun oddiy yozma uslub",
      "meaning_en": "Plain written style (diaries, articles, blogs)",
      "explanation_md": "**한다체** — **yozma nutq** uslubi: kundalik, maqola, kitob, blog, yangilik sarlavhalari. U hech kimga murojaat qilmaydi, shuning uchun hurmat ham, \"sen\" ham emas — neytral.\n\n**설날에는 떡국을 먹는다.** — *Sollalda ttokguk yeyiladi.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n| | Shakl | Misol |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fe'l, 받침siz | **-ㄴ다** | 간다, 쓴다, 빈다 |\n| Fe'l, 받침 bilan | **-는다** | 먹는다, 입는다 |\n| Sifat | **-다** (lug'at shakli) | 다르다, 비슷하다 |\n| Ot | **N(이)다** | 설날이다, 전통이다 |\n| O'tgan | **-았/었다** | 먹었다, 갔다, 특별했다 |\n| Kelasi | **-(으)ㄹ 것이다** | 갈 것이다 |\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- **ㄹ** fe'llar: ㄹ tushib **-ㄴ다**: 살다 → **산다**, 만들다 → **만든다**, 빌다 → **빈다**\n- **있다/없다** → **있다/없다** (o'zgarmaydi)\n- Og'zaki suhbatda ishlatilmaydi — faqat yozuvda (yoki o'zingizga gapirganda).",
      "explanation_md_en": "**한다체** is the **plain written style**: diaries, articles, books, blogs, headlines. It addresses no one in particular, so it's neither polite nor casual — just neutral.\n\n**설날에는 떡국을 먹는다.** — *On Seollal people eat tteokguk.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n| | Form | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Verb, no 받침 | **-ㄴ다** | 간다, 쓴다, 빈다 |\n| Verb, with 받침 | **-는다** | 먹는다, 입는다 |\n| Adjective | **-다** (dictionary form) | 다르다, 비슷하다 |\n| Noun | **N(이)다** | 설날이다, 전통이다 |\n| Past | **-았/었다** | 먹었다, 갔다, 특별했다 |\n| Future | **-(으)ㄹ 것이다** | 갈 것이다 |\n\n### Remember\n\n- **ㄹ** verbs drop ㄹ + **-ㄴ다**: 살다 → **산다**, 만들다 → **만든다**, 빌다 → **빈다**\n- **있다/없다** stay **있다/없다**\n- It's not used in conversation — only in writing (or talking to yourself).",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Fe'l (받침siz)",
          "condition_en": "Verb (no 받침)",
          "rule": "-ㄴ다",
          "example": "간다, 쓴다"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Fe'l (받침 bor)",
          "condition_en": "Verb (with 받침)",
          "rule": "-는다",
          "example": "먹는다, 입는다"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Sifat / Ot",
          "condition_en": "Adjective / Noun",
          "rule": "-다 / N(이)다",
          "example": "다르다, 설날이다"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "O'tgan",
          "condition_en": "Past",
          "rule": "-았/었다",
          "example": "먹었다, 특별했다"
        }
