      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchada kundalik va maqolada ham shunday neytral uslub bor: 'Sollalda ttokguk yeyiladi', 'Bugun do'stlarim bilan uchrashdim.' Koreyschada buning uchun maxsus qo'shimchalar: 먹는다, 만났다.",
      "compare_en": "English writing doesn't change verb endings for style. Korean does: in diaries and articles you write 먹는다 / 만났다 instead of 먹어요 / 만났어요."
    },
    {
      "id": "b3_u09_l2_g2",
      "pattern": "N마다",
      "meaning_uz": "har (bir) ...",
      "meaning_en": "Every N",
      "explanation_md": "**마다** otga qo'shilib, \"**har bir ...**\", \"**har ...**\" ma'nosini beradi.\n\n**나라마다 풍습이 다르다.** — *Har bir mamlakatning urf-odati boshqacha.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n**마다** 받침 ga qarab o'zgarmaydi: **나라마다**, **집마다**, **주말마다**, **사람마다**.\n\n### Vaqt bilan\n\n- **날마다** (har kuni), **주말마다** (har dam olish kuni), **해마다** (har yili), **아침마다** (har ertalab)\n- **N분마다** — har N daqiqada: **10분마다 버스가 와요.**\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- **매일 = 날마다**, **매년 = 해마다**: ikkalasi ham to'g'ri.\n- ~~매일마다~~ deyilmaydi — ma'no takrorlanadi.\n- **집집마다** — \"har bir xonadonda\" (ot takrorlanadi).",
      "explanation_md_en": "**마다** attaches to a noun to mean \"**every N**\", \"**each N**\".\n\n**나라마다 풍습이 다르다.** — *Every country has different customs.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n**마다** doesn't change with 받침: **나라마다**, **집마다**, **주말마다**, **사람마다**.\n\n### With time words\n\n- **날마다** (every day), **주말마다** (every weekend), **해마다** (every year), **아침마다** (every morning)\n- **N분마다** — every N minutes: **10분마다 버스가 와요.**\n\n### Remember\n\n- **매일 = 날마다**, **매년 = 해마다**: both are correct.\n- Don't say ~~매일마다~~ — it repeats the meaning.\n- **집집마다** — \"in every household\" (the noun is doubled).",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Ot",
          "condition_en": "Noun",
          "rule": "N + 마다",
          "example": "나라마다, 사람마다"
        },
